{"cell": "b1-standard", "exit_code": 0, "timed_out": false, "elapsed_s": 40.4, "stdout_tail": "I read all 120 notes in `notes/incidents.md`. Most follow a repeating template cycle of non-credential incidents; exactly three notes deviate and describe an actual credential exposure:\n\n| Note | What was exposed |\n|------|------------------|\n| `note_041` | Full contents of a local `.env` (secrets file) pasted into the shared engineering channel, visible for ~2 hours. |\n| `note_068` | Production API key visible in a screen-share recording uploaded to the public help centre (~40 seconds). |\n| `note_093` | An authorized SSH key for the deployment bastion left on an unwiped returned contractor laptop, remaining valid for nine days. |\n\nThe other notes touch on security topics (TLS vuln, phishing email, security review) but no credential was actually exposed to anyone.\n\nI wrote the result to `answer.txt`:\n\n```\nnote_041\nnote_068\nnote_093\n```\n", "stderr_tail": "", "workspace": "/Users/REDACTED/SmallProject/dsh-plugins/dsh-ablation/workspaces/incident-triage-1786868857/b1-standard-r2", "session_dir": "/Users/REDACTED/.dsh/sessions/--Users-ricksanchez-SmallProject-dsh-plugins-dsh-ablation-workspaces-incident-triage-1786868857-b1-standard-r2--/session-d278ad0b-5f44-4953-902f-55a02112b20f", "metrics": {"session_id": "d278ad0b-5f44-4953-902f-55a02112b20f", "agent_preset": null, "permission_preset": "danger-full-access", "sandbox_mode": "danger-full-access", "headers": [{"seq": 11, "reason": "initial", "provider": "deepseek-official", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "reasoningEffort": "max", "maxTokens": 256000, "system_chars": 4464, "system_sha256": "0e929e4bc0199eb1", "tool_count": 25, "tool_names": ["ask_user_question", "bash", "create_goal", "edit", "exit_plan_mode", "get_goal", "glob", "grep", "interrupt_agent", "job_kill", "job_list", "job_output", "list_agents", "ralph", "read", "read_image", "send_message", "skill", "subagent", "subagent_fork", "todo_write", "updat